  "result": "I fixed the queue in `src/queue.js` so it follows the contract in its header comment, and `npm test` now passes (5 tests, 0 failed). I haven't committed anything.\n\nI found four causes behind your three reports:\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never decremented `running`, so the slot was never freed. A job that threw synchronously, or returned a plain value instead of a promise, also broke `fn().then(...)`.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** the idle check looked only at `pending`, so it could resolve while jobs were still running. It now requires both `pending` and `running` to be zero.\n- **One job at a time after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `next()` started at most one job per call. It now loops until every free slot is filled.\n\nI added three regression tests to `test/queue.test.js`:\n\n- A queue keeps going after a job fails, whether it rejects or throws synchronously.\n- `onIdle()` waits for running jobs and resolves at once when the queue is already idle.\n- With concurrency 4, `resume()` starts four jobs and leaves the fifth pending.\n\nI didn't run the new tests against the old code, so I haven't confirmed they fail without the fix.",
